I'm treating this as a ballot for the two voting advisors. I'm not answering the executor myself and I'm not asking the operator, and nothing gets built on step 6 until the vote returns. Messages to the operator are in Russian, because §15 makes Russian the operator's language. Everything between agents is in English.

**1. Bash, foreground (read-only, takes seconds)**
```bash
herdr agent get wgka; herdr agent get adv-codex; herdr agent get adv-fable     # none focused?
herdr agent read wgka --source visible; herdr agent read adv-codex --source visible; herdr agent read adv-fable --source visible   # context usage
WT=~/work/ccs.ansible/.claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive
git -C "$WT" rev-parse HEAD; git -C "$WT" status --short
git -C "$WT" grep -nE '10\.77\.1\.(0/24|0/25|128/25)'                           # evidence for the ballot context
```

**2. Write `$ORCH/quorum/ballot-<n>.md`** (`<n>` is the next free ballot number)
```
B<n> — Source allow-list for the WireGuard keepalive relay
  Context: ~/work/ccs.ansible, worktree .claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive, branch feat/wg-keepalive-relay @ <HEAD>;
    plan <path>, step 6 of 11 (steps 7-11 build on this value); design doc <path>. VPN /24 = 10.77.1.0/24;
    WireGuard clients = 10.77.1.128/25; 10.77.1.0/25 = <assignment, path:line>; front-door allow-list =
    10.77.1.0/24 (<path:line>). Value lives in versioned config. Canary ccs-it, then ccs-ops. Rules: quorum/protocol.md.
  a) Allow 10.77.1.128/25. Admits the WireGuard range only; 10.77.1.0/25 cannot reach the relay. Differs from
     the front-door value. Cost if wrong: a keepalive sender outside the /25 is dropped. Rollback: change one value on main, redeploy.
  b) Allow 10.77.1.0/24. Admits every VPN client, including 10.77.1.0/25. Same value as the front door.
     Cost if wrong: hosts in 10.77.1.0/25 reach the relay port. Rollback: change one value on main, redeploy.
Read-only; change nothing. Reply in English, one line:  B<n>: <letter> — <rationale>   (or  B<n>: X: <proposal>)
```

**3. Bash, background, three calls in one message**
```bash
herdr agent prompt adv-codex "$(cat "$ORCH/quorum/ballot-<n>.md")" --wait --timeout 1800000; herdr agent read adv-codex --source recent-unwrapped --lines 200 > "$ORCH/inbox/adv-codex.last"
herdr agent prompt adv-fable "$(cat "$ORCH/quorum/ballot-<n>.md")" --wait --timeout 1800000; herdr agent read adv-fable --source recent-unwrapped --lines 200 > "$ORCH/inbox/adv-fable.last"
herdr agent prompt wgka "Step 6's allow-list is ballot B<n>, now with the voting advisors. Do not implement step 6 or any later step; write no provisional or placeholder value. Commit any uncommitted work, stop, and reply in English with one line: phase, branch, head SHA, next step. I will relay the decision." --wait --timeout 600000; herdr agent read wgka --source recent-unwrapped --lines 200 > "$ORCH/inbox/wgka.last"
```

**4. Update the backlog.** The task entry gets `blocked-on: B<n>` and `next step: ballot B<n>`, and B<n> is added under decisions as open. Then run `bash build-backlog.sh` and republish the Artifact at the same path.

**5. Status to the operator (chat, verbatim)**
> **Статус — WireGuard keepalive relay, 01:40**
> **Сейчас:** wgka на шаге 6 из 11. Нужно выбрать source allow-list для релея: только WireGuard `10.77.1.128/25` или вся VPN-сеть `10.77.1.0/24`. Это решают голосующие советники: бюллетень B<n> ушёл adv-codex и adv-fable. Шаги 7–11 строятся на этом значении, поэтому wgka ждёт решения 2/2 и пока ничего не пишет.
> **Дальше:** после 2/2 wgka сделает шаги 7–11. Потом ревью свежей сессией Codex на точном SHA и моя проверка на том же SHA. Мерж и go на канарейку решают советники голосованием. Деплой на ccs-it идёт только из смёрженного `main`: dry run, реальный прогон, проверка, повторный прогон с нулём изменений. Если советники разойдутся, это будет ваш опрос. Он дождётся утра, будить не буду, а канарейка сдвинется. Раскатка на ccs-ops — ваш опрос после приёмки.
> **От вас:** (1) сейчас: один опрос ниже. (2) Утром, когда в чате будет «канарейка на ccs-it развёрнута», сделайте приёмку. Подключитесь своим WireGuard-профилем и запустите `ping -i 0.2 172.27.96.2`. Через 3 минуты остановите его (Ctrl+C) и вставьте сюда последние три строки вывода.
> Бэклог: <artifact URL>

**6. AskUserQuestion**, one question:
"Не давать Mac уснуть этой ночью, чтобы канарейка на ccs-it прошла?"
- **(Рекомендую) Да:** я запущу `caffeinate -is -t 28800`. Mac должен быть на зарядке. Во сне Mac обрывает ходы агентов и блокирует keychain, и тогда SSH на ccs-it не пройдёт.
- **Нет:** пусть спит, канарейка переезжает на утро.

**7. When the notifications arrive**
- Read the `.last` files and write `ballot-<n>.results.md`.
- If wgka's context is at 50% or more, compact it now while it is parked (background, `--wait --timeout 300000`).
- If the vote is 2/2: relay the result to wgka as a background prompt with `--wait` and a time box for steps 7–11. Update the backlog and name B<n> in the next status.
- If the vote splits: the poll waits for the morning and wgka stays parked.

**Why**
- The allow-list is a choice between alternatives, so the two voting advisors decide it. It isn't mine to decide, it isn't the executor's, and it isn't one of the operator's four kinds of decision. That also fits their "no trivia".
- I removed the executor's recommendation and its one-sided reasons ("only WireGuard sends", "simpler") from the ballot. Each option has its own facts and the same cost-if-wrong and rollback lines, because the value ends up on a live site.
- Steps 7–11 all build on step 6, so wgka parks. "Canary tonight" doesn't justify building on a guess.
- The merge and the canary go are also votes, so the overnight path doesn't need the operator.
- The acceptance test needs the operator's hands, so it's an instruction for the morning, not a question. The status says plainly that acceptance happens in the morning.
- Keeping the Mac awake is the operator's decision. A sleeping Mac would end tonight's canary, so I'm asking now, while they're still awake.
